Oh gosh! Please forgive me, @JohnWM! My eyes are bad, and map I was looking at small: New Brunswick is on Atlantic Daylight Time (9:06pm). It's Golfe-du-St.-Laurent regional municipality, in Quebec, which remains on Atlantic Standard Time (8:06pm) throughout the year.

New Brunswick is considering adopting Daylight Saving Time throughout the year, but only if the United States and/or the other Canadian provinces do likewise. So sayeth Wikipedia.

