@Bill in Yokohama
The linguist Mario Pei made an interesting observation: in Ancient, and Modern, Greek, the sound a sheep makes is written as βῆ. In Ancient Greek, this was pronounced "bay," but in Modern Greek, more like "vee"; the sheep, however, haven't changed their pronunciation.

Mario Pei used to come occasionally in the crossword, when the architect was busy elsewhere.

